# The active baseline is cluster-local and must never be committed.
#
# `default` is a symlink to a copy of logs/<node> taken from a node validated on
# THIS cluster. Commit it and every tarball drop overwrites the headnode's real
# baseline with a pointer to a node that does not exist here -- node_health.sh
# then diffs every check against a missing file, every node fails every check,
# and report_health.sh reports a cluster-wide hardware fault that is really one
# bad symlink. That is exactly what a committed
# `default -> /home/cmods/bringup/valid-config/a01-11-s1-dgx-01-c01` did.
#
# Create the baseline on the cluster with admin_set-baseline.sh, never in git.
# This directory is tracked (via this file) only so the tarball still unpacks a
# valid-config/ for admin_set-baseline.sh to write into.
*
!.gitignore
